  "reason": "The current best is config_032 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, concat) at 0.688. The image modality is very weak standalone (0.208 with resnet50), yet it still contributes ~3.5% when concatenated with the strong RNA signal. This raises the question of whether a weighted fusion—allowing the model to learn modality-specific importance—can outperform simple concatenation by downweighting the weaker image features. Config_033 changes only the fusion method (concat→weighted) while keeping all other settings identical to config_032, making it a clean, single-variable comparison. This is the best use of experiment 9 because it directly exploits the strongest result with a minimal, well-motivated modification; if it improves on 0.688, we secure a better final answer, and if it does not, we retain one experiment to explore the image-encoder axis (e.g., ViT-L via config_038)."
}

